## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
Severity: MEDIUM  
Broadcom is a fab-lite semiconductor company, relying heavily on foundries like TSMC for manufacturing. This creates exposure to foundry capacity constraints and pricing volatility. Its customer concentration in the data center market (e.g., Meta, Google Cloud) makes it vulnerable to capex cycles. While its ecosystem relationships (e.g., VMware, Arista) provide some stability, the reliance on external foundries and cyclical end-markets elevates risk.  

---

## 4. Investment Thesis & Peer Comparison
Bull Case: Broadcom’s leadership in AI and cloud infrastructure, coupled with strong FCF growth, positions it for long-term success. Its ecosystem relationships and R&D investments drive competitive moats.  

Bear Case: Dependency on foundries and cyclical data center demand exposes it to capex downturns. Elevated D/E ratio and near-term valuation pressures raise risks.  

Verdict: BUY — Scale-In on Pullback (entry $313.5)  

